{
  "id": "34004_kibamu",
  "headword": "{黄|き}ばむ",
  "reading": "きばむ",
  "romaji": "kibamu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to turn yellow; to yellow with age",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to turn yellowish (with age or stains)",
      "explanation": "For something white, such as cloth, paper or teeth, to take on a yellowish tinge over time."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "34004_kibamu_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦シャツ→シャツ：01052_shatsu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{黄|き}ばんだ。",
      "english": "The shirt has yellowed.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "34004_kibamu_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{古|ふる}い→古い：00488_furui⟧{本|ほん}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦ページ→ページ：02961_peeji⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{黄|き}ばんで⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧。",
      "english": "The pages of the old book have turned yellow.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "34004_kibamu_ex3",
      "japanese": "⟦{白|しろ}い→白い：00587_shiroi⟧Tシャツ⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{襟|えり}→襟：06487_eri⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{汗|あせ}→汗：02173_ase⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{黄|き}ばんでしまった⟦の→の：09472_no⟧で、⟦{漂白剤|ひょうはくざい}→漂白剤：07035_hyouhakuzai⟧につけた。",
      "english": "The collar of my white T-shirt yellowed with sweat, so I soaked it in bleach.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Mostly in the past or て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ form for the resulting state: {黄|き}ばんだ⟦{紙|かみ}→紙：00712_kami⟧ (yellowed paper), {黄|き}ばんで⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧. Usually said of white things (cloth, paper, teeth); also of leaves turning yellowish (⟦{葉|は}→葉：02241_ha⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{黄|き}ばむ).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Intransitive; no transitive partner\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{黄色|きいろ}→黄色：02870_kiiro⟧: yellow\n- ⟦{色|いろ}あせる→色あせる：16726_iroaseru⟧: to fade (loss of color rather than yellowing)",
